@.str.99 = private unnamed_addr constant [2756 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Build the default package from the flake in the current directory:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build\0A  ```\0A\0A* Build and run GNU Hello from the `nixpkgs` flake:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build nixpkgs#hello\0A  # ./result/bin/hello\0A  Hello, world!\0A  ```\0A\0A* Build GNU Hello and Cowsay, leaving two result symlinks:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build nixpkgs#hello nixpkgs#cowsay\0A  # ls -l result*\0A  lrwxrwxrwx 1 \E2\80\A6 result -> /nix/store/v5sv61sszx301i0x6xysaqzla09nksnd-hello-2.10\0A  lrwxrwxrwx 1 \E2\80\A6 result-1 -> /nix/store/rkfrm0z6x6jmi7d3gsmma4j53h15mg33-cowsay-3.03+dfsg2\0A  ```\0A\0A* Build GNU Hello and print the resulting store path.\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build nixpkgs#hello --print-out-paths\0A  /nix/store/v5sv61sszx301i0x6xysaqzla09nksnd-hello-2.10\0A  ```\0A\0A* Build a specific output:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build nixpkgs#glibc.dev\0A  # ls -ld ./result-dev\0A  lrwxrwxrwx 1 \E2\80\A6 ./result-dev -> /nix/store/dkm3gwl0xrx0wrw6zi5x3px3lpgjhlw4-glibc-2.32-dev\0A  ```\0A\0A* Build attribute `build.x86_64-linux` from (non-flake) Nix expression\0A  `release.nix`:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build --file release.nix build.x86_64-linux\0A  ```\0A\0A* Build a NixOS system configuration from a flake, and make a profile\0A  point to the result:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build --profile /nix/var/nix/profiles/system \\\0A      ~/my-configurations#nixosConfigurations.machine.config.system.build.toplevel\0A  ```\0A\0A  (This is essentially what `nixos-rebuild` does.)\0A\0A* Build an expression specified on the command line:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build --impure --expr \\\0A      'with import <nixpkgs> {};\0A       runCommand \22foo\22 {\0A         buildInputs = [ hello ];\0A       }\0A       \22hello > $out\22'\0A  # cat ./result\0A  Hello, world!\0A  ```\0A\0A  Note that `--impure` is needed because we're using `<nixpkgs>`,\0A  which relies on the `$NIX_PATH` environment variable.\0A\0A* Fetch a store path from the configured substituters, if it doesn't\0A  already exist:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix build /nix/store/rkfrm0z6x6jmi7d3gsmma4j53h15mg33-cowsay-3.03+dfsg2\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0A`nix build` builds the specified *installables*. [Installables](./nix.md#installables) that\0Aresolve to derivations are built (or substituted if possible). Store\0Apath installables are substituted.\0A\0AUnless `--no-link` is specified, after a successful build, it creates\0Asymlinks to the store paths of the installables. These symlinks have\0Athe prefix `./result` by default; this can be overridden using the\0A`--out-link` option. Each symlink has a suffix `-<N>-<outname>`, where\0A*N* is the index of the installable (with the left-most installable\0Ahaving index 0), and *outname* is the symbolic derivation output name\0A(e.g. `bin`, `dev` or `lib`). `-<N>` is omitted if *N* = 0, and\0A`-<outname>` is omitted if *outname* = `out` (denoting the default\0Aoutput).\0A\0A\00", align 1
